Scripted tests for the Vue GUI
==============================

The .scm files build test widgets (they are loaded with -x) and the .script
files drive them with synthetic events, see the "Scripted events" section
of vue_gui.cpp for the commands. Coordinates are window points relative to
the content area of the target window; they match the layouts of the .scm
files in this directory.

Run from the source directory, e.g.

  export TEXMACS_PATH=$PWD/TeXmacs
  export TEXMACS_VUE_SNAPSHOT=/tmp/vue-snapshots      # PNG of every window redraw
  export TEXMACS_VUE_SCRIPT=src/Plugins/Vue/tests/widgets.script
  TeXmacs/bin/texmacs.bin -x '(load "src/Plugins/Vue/tests/widgets.scm")'

and check the standard output for the callbacks (choice:, enum:, got: ...)
and the named snapshots (t0.png, t1-enum-open.png, ...). The catalogue of
the tests, and what each of them is checking, is in docs/vue-testing.md.

popup.scm and pre-edit.scm are empty ((noop)): those two scripts drive the
editor of the main window and need no widget of their own, but a .scm is
loaded for every test so that the -x argument is uniform.
